  <h1 class="mb-5 mt-0 font-serif text-4xl font-semibold leading-tight text-base-content sm:text-[2.8rem]">Social Casino Index Data and API</h1>

  <div class="answer-first">
    <span class="af-label">In short</span>
    <p><strong>The Social Casino Index toplist is free to use as JSON or through an MCP server.</strong> It has the same order and values as the homepage, and every value links to the dated operator source it came from.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>JSON feed</h2>
  <p><a href="/api/toplist.json"><code>https://socialcasinoindex.com/api/toplist.json</code></a> returns the current toplist and state offer policy. It needs no key and allows cross-origin requests. The <a href="/api/openapi.json">OpenAPI description</a> documents every field.</p>
  <p>Each casino has a position, a one-line summary, and these facts where the operator publishes them: signup bonus, first-purchase offer, daily reward, payout time, and cash, gift-card or general redemption minimums. Each fact carries its source URL and observation time. Last checked: {{ benchmarks.toplist.lastCheckedAt | readableDate }}.</p>

  <h2>MCP server</h2>
  <p>AI assistants can query the toplist at <code>https://mcp.socialcasinoindex.com/mcp</code> (Streamable HTTP, no authentication). It is listed in the official MCP Registry as <code>com.socialcasinoindex/toplist</code>. Tools:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>get_top_social_casinos</code>: the toplist in homepage order.</li>
    <li><code>get_social_casino</code>: one casino by name.</li>
    <li><code>check_state_availability</code>: the offer policy for a US state.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>License and citation</h2>
  <p>The data is licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>. You may reuse it if you credit Social Casino Index and link this page. Suggested citation:</p>
  <p><code>Social Casino Index (Sweeps Brief LLC). Social Casino Index toplist. https://socialcasinoindex.com/data/</code></p>
  <p>Operator names and offer terms belong to the operators. Values describe published terms on the observation date and can change. Order follows the <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>; affiliate status never affects it. See the <a href="/disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
